---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalNotice from '../components/LegalNotice.astro';
import { TERMS_VERSION, TRIAL_DAYS, longDate, operator } from '../lib/site';
---
<Base title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using AlgoMinutes, the AI meeting-notes app from Algorythmos Pty Ltd.">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="meta">Version {TERMS_VERSION} · last updated {longDate(TERMS_VERSION)}</p>
    <LegalNotice />

    <p>
      These terms are an agreement between you and {operator.name} (ABN {operator.abn}, "we", "us") for your use of
      AlgoMinutes: the app, this website and the service behind them. By using AlgoMinutes, including as a guest, you
      agree to them and to our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>. When you sign in with Apple or Google, the app
      records which versions you accepted.
    </p>

    <h2 id="service">1. The service</h2>
    <p>
      We keep improving AlgoMinutes, so features may change or be limited, as section 9 describes. Keep your own copy
      of anything you can't afford to lose.
    </p>

    <h2 id="eligibility">2. Who can use AlgoMinutes</h2>
    <p>You must be at least 13, and old enough where you live to agree to these terms yourself.</p>

    <h2 id="accounts">3. Your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Sign in with Apple or Google, or continue as a guest. A guest account lives on one device; to keep its notes, create an account from Settings. If you sign out as a guest, you can't get back into that guest account.</li>
      <li>Keep access to your sign-in account secure. You're responsible for what happens in your AlgoMinutes account.</li>
      <li>You can delete your account at any time in Settings → Delete my account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="consent">4. Recording other people</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>You're responsible for having permission to record.</strong> Recording laws differ between places, and
      many require the consent of everyone being recorded. Tell people before you record them, and don't record
      anyone secretly or where the law doesn't allow it. The notice AlgoMinutes shows before recording is a reminder,
      not legal advice.
    </p>

    <h2 id="content">5. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      Your recordings and notes are yours. You give us a licence to store, copy and process them (including with the
      AI services described in our Privacy Policy) only to provide AlgoMinutes to you. The licence ends when you delete
      them, apart from backups, which expire as the Privacy Policy describes. You confirm you have the rights you need
      in what you upload.
    </p>

    <h2 id="ai-output">6. AI output</h2>
    <p>
      Transcripts, summaries, action items and answers are produced automatically and can be incomplete or wrong,
      including about who said what. Check anything important against the recording before you rely on it. AlgoMinutes
      doesn't give legal, medical, financial or other professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2 id="use">7. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Don't use AlgoMinutes to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>record people unlawfully, or to harass, threaten or harm anyone;</li>
      <li>upload content you don't have the right to, or that's unlawful;</li>
      <li>break, overload, probe or get around the security or limits of the service, or access other people's data;</li>
      <li>copy, resell or reverse engineer the service, except where the law allows it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="fees">8. Free minutes and AlgoMinutes Pro</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Free minutes.</strong> Every account gets a number of free recording minutes each month, shown in the
      app. A new account on an iPhone that hasn't had one before may also get a free trial: more minutes for {TRIAL_DAYS} days,
      after which the account goes back to its free minutes. We allow one trial per iPhone, and use
      Apple's DeviceCheck to check that, as our <a href="/privacy#trial">Privacy Policy</a> explains. The free minutes
      and the trial aren't a trial of a subscription: they don't need payment details, nothing is charged, and they
      never turn into a paid subscription.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>AlgoMinutes Pro</strong> is an auto-renewing subscription that gives you more minutes. You buy it in the
      AlgoMinutes app through the App Store. Before you buy, the app shows the price and how often you'll be billed;
      payment is charged to your Apple Account when you confirm the purchase.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Renewal.</strong> Pro renews automatically at the end of each period, and Apple charges your Apple Account for the next period within the 24 hours before it begins, unless you cancel at least 24 hours before the current period ends.</li>
      <li><strong>Managing and cancelling.</strong> Manage or cancel Pro in your Apple account settings: on your iPhone, Settings, your name, then Subscriptions (or from the app's Settings). Cancelling stops the next renewal; you keep Pro until the end of the period you've paid for. Deleting your AlgoMinutes account doesn't cancel an App Store subscription.</li>
      <li><strong>Refunds.</strong> Apple handles payment for App Store purchases, so refunds are requested from Apple under its policies.</li>
      <li><strong>Price changes.</strong> If we change Pro's price, Apple tells you before the new price applies, as its rules require.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Purchases in the App Store are also governed by Apple's terms. Nothing in this section limits your rights under
      the Australian Consumer Law or your local consumer laws, as section 11 explains.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes-service">9. Changes and availability</h2>
    <p>
      We may change or discontinue features. We'll give you reasonable notice of a change that significantly reduces
      what you can do, and the chance to export or delete your notes before we end the service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="termination">10. Ending this agreement</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop using AlgoMinutes and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or close an account that
      seriously or repeatedly breaks these terms, or where the law requires, and we'll tell you why unless we're not
      allowed to.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">11. Our responsibility to you</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing in these terms excludes, restricts or modifies any right or remedy you have under the Australian Consumer
      Law or other laws that can't be excluded. Our goods and services come with guarantees that can't be excluded
      under the Australian Consumer Law.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apart from those rights, and to the extent the law allows: AlgoMinutes is provided "as is"; we
      aren't liable for indirect or consequential loss, or for loss of data you could have kept a copy of; and our
      total liability to you is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim (or, where the
      Australian Consumer Law applies, to supplying the service again or paying for it to be supplied again).
    </p>

    <h2 id="law">12. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia, and you and we submit to its courts. If you
      live elsewhere, you keep the protections of your local consumer laws.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">13. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      When we change these terms we update the version and date above. Before a significant change takes effect,
      we'll tell you in the app or by email. If you keep using AlgoMinutes after that, the new terms apply; if you
      don't agree, you can delete your account.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">14. Contact</h2>
    <p>{operator.name}, {operator.locality}. Email <a href={`mailto:${operator.support}`}>{operator.support}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
